FEATURES, CUI ACCESS, MONGO COMMANDSCREATE DB, COLLECTION DOCUMENTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------

=>Features of MongoDB
    ->Schema-less Database: MongoDB is a NoSQL database, which means it doesn't require a predefined schema.

    ->Scalability: It scales horizontally using sharding.Horizontal sharding refers to taking a single MySQL database and partitioning the data across several database servers, each with an identical schema.

    ->Performance: Its document-oriented data model allows for faster read/write operations.

    ->Flexibility: JSON-like documents are easy to store and query.

    ->Indexing: Supports secondary indexes to improve search performance.

    ->Aggregation: Powerful aggregation framework for data analysis and transformation.

    ->Replication: High availability with replica sets.

    =====================================================

=>Command-Line Interface (CUI) Access

    To access the MongoDB shell, open your terminal and type:

    ------------------------------------------
    mongosh
    ------------------------------------------

    This will launch the interactive MongoDB shell where you can run various commands.

    MongoDB Commands to Create Database, Collection, and Documents
    Here's a quick guide to creating a database, a collection within it, and adding documents to that collection.

    1. Create a Database:

    -----------------------------------------

    use myDatabase

    -----------------------------------------

    note:This will switch to the database myDatabase. If it doesn't exist, MongoDB will create it.

    2. Create a Collection:

    -----------------------------------------

    db.createCollection("myCollection")

    -----------------------------------------
    note:This will create a collection named myCollection.


    3.Insert Documents:

    ->for single data
    ------------------------------------------
    
    db.myCollection.insertOne({name: "ram sharma", age: 30, city: "Indore"})

    ------------------------------------------

    -> for multiple data
    -------------------------------------------
    db.myCollection.insertMany([
        {name: "ram sharma", age: 25, city: "Indore"},
        {name: "mohan yadav", age: 35, city: "Indore"}
    ])

    -------------------------------------------